Docker Use Cases — Short & Simple
1. Microservices Architecture

Docker runs different parts of an application in separate containers.

Benefit: Easy to develop, deploy, and scale each service independently.

2. CI/CD

Docker provides the same environment for development, testing, and production.

Benefit: Reduces errors and makes deployment faster.

3. Cloud Migration

Docker packages applications so they can easily be moved to the cloud.

Benefit: Applications can run consistently on different cloud platforms.

4. Scalable Web Applications

Docker allows multiple containers to run the same web application.

Benefit: Easy to increase or decrease application capacity based on traffic.

5. Testing and QA

Docker creates separate and consistent environments for testing.

Benefit: Makes testing faster and more reliable.

6. Machine Learning & AI

Docker packages ML models with Python, libraries, and dependencies.

Benefit: Easy deployment, scaling, and consistent ML environments.

7. API Development and Deployment

Docker packages APIs with all their required dependencies.

Benefit: Easy development, testing, deployment, and scaling.